gcm/live-draw: a draw that samples its own render target reads it even when other surfaces share the address
(LD_NO_SELF_EXACT=1 old).

Symptom (Killzone 2, in-level pause menu): the whole screen goes white with a dark vignette within a few frames of
pressing Start; the HUD crosshair stays; the game keeps running.

Cause: the colour grade (Killzone 2 1.29, fragment program at loc 1 0x002D5980) draws into the 2560x720 lit-scene
target at 0x1E30000 and samples that same target (unit 0, A8R8G8B8 2560x720) plus the depth and a 64x64 depth-by-value
LUT in main memory. The texture-to-surface lookup skips the bound target and takes the best other surface at the
address; only when there is none does it fall back to the target's feedback copy. While paused, the game also renders
into 0x1E30000 as a 320x180 surface (bloom chain) and a 1280x720 one (the final composite), so the grade found one of
those, sampled last frame's picture, and graded it again each frame. The picture converges to the LUT's brightest near entry
(248, 255, 233), the vignette comes after it. Seen in kz2-r41-pause3 (draw dump frame 4459): the grade's input at
0x1E30000 2560x720 has mean RGB (29, 38, 46) before the draw, the composite input after it is flat (248, 255, 233).

Fix: a texture whose address and size are the bound target's is a self-read: it takes the feedback copy whatever
else shares the address (the size rule the lookup already applies, now including the target). Other aliases keep
the old rule. "[self-read]" logs the first redirections (and a count every 65536). In kz2-r41-pause4 the first one
is at frame 4429 (flip 4430 at 174.6 s, Start pressed at pad time 175 s), none before the pause: the alias exists
only while paused. Written for this port.
Host test: none (the rule sits in the walker's bind loop; verified in Proton, see the runtime notes).
Upstream candidate (any title whose pass reads its target while another surface sits at the same address).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0: context and offsets only.

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c b/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
--- a/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
@@ -13663,7 +13663,35 @@ static void sink_end_impl(void* user, const rsx_dispatch* r)
                   ncall++;
               }
           } }
-        if (!zeta_pref) { u32 best_gen = 0;
+        /* KZ2 patch 2097: a texture that IS the bound render target (same address and the target's own size) reads
+         * the target, through the feedback copy below, even when other surfaces share the address. The loop
+         * skips the target, so with another surface at the address (Killzone 2's pause screen: its final
+         * composite makes a 1280x720 surface at 0x1E30000, the 2560x720 lit-scene target of the colour grade
+         * that reads itself) the grade sampled that other surface, last frame's graded picture, and graded it
+         * again every frame until the screen was the LUT's white end. LD_NO_SELF_EXACT=1 = old behaviour. */
+        int self_exact = 0;
+        { static int off = -1;
+          if (off < 0) off = getenv("LD_NO_SELF_EXACT") ? 1 : 0;
+          const surface_t* tg = target < g.n_surfaces ? &g.surfaces[target] : NULL;
+          self_exact = !off && !zeta_pref && tg && tg->location == t.location && tg->offset == t.offset &&
+                       tg->w == t.width && tg->h == t.height;
+          if (self_exact) {
+              static u32 nlog; static u64 nredir;
+              int other = -1;
+              for (u32 i = 0; i < g.n_surfaces; i++)
+                  if (i != target && g.surfaces[i].location == t.location && g.surfaces[i].offset == t.offset) other = (int)i;
+              if (other >= 0) {
+                  nredir++;
+                  if (nlog < 16 || (nredir & 0xFFFFu) == 0) {
+                      nlog++;
+                      fprintf(stderr, "[self-read] f=%u unit %u tex %u:0x%08X %ux%u fmt=0x%02X is target %u: feedback "
+                              "copy, not surface[%d] %ux%u (%llu redirected)\n", g_ld_frames, u, t.location, t.offset,
+                              t.width, t.height, t.format, target, other, g.surfaces[other].w, g.surfaces[other].h,
+                              (unsigned long long)nredir);
+                  }
+              }
+          } }
+        if (!zeta_pref && !self_exact) { u32 best_gen = 0;
           for (u32 i = 0; i < g.n_surfaces; i++) {
               const surface_t* sf_i = &g.surfaces[i];
               if (sf_i->location != t.location || sf_i->offset != t.offset ||
